  designNotes: '2026-08-26, real playtested bug ("每次都是劈砍結束後劍才紅") - the earlier
    note here correctly identified the real strike at t=0.59 normalized (motion
    spike), but the hitWindows array below it had somehow ended up with 0.78-0.93
    instead of the 0.55-0.68 the note itself describes - a stale/mistyped value,
    not a measurement error. Re-measured properly this time via
    AnimationMode.SampleAnimationClip, tracking BladeHitbox position/speed
    relative to root across the whole clip: the blade is held raised overhead
    (height 4.3-5.2 relative to root) from t=0.10 to t=0.55, then a sharp speed
    spike (peak 63.9 units/s at t=0.576) crashes it down through a real
    front-facing, full-body-height sweep (forward 1.3-2.7, height dropping from
    4.5 down to -0.2 relative to root) across t=0.56-0.65, settling near-ground
    by t=0.66. 0.78-0.93 was entirely inside the slow recovery AFTER that crash
    (speed 3.5-10 there, blade already lifting back up) - same "window fires
    after the swing already happened" bug as Wushi_Attack_SwordJudgment. measured
    is 1 this time.'
